error: `climb` instantiates itself endlessly
  --> 011_instantiation_depth.kira:16:5
   16 |     climb[n + 1]()
      |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ generic instantiation is too deep
  help: Each call with a new compile-time argument compiles a new copy of `climb`, so a body that calls itself at a *different* argument every time (`climb[n]` calling `climb[n + 1]`, say) never bottoms out. Recurse at an argument that eventually repeats, or make the recursion an ordinary runtime one over a parameter you don't change.
